{
  "title": "10: Yunus يونس",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nالٓر تِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ الْكِتٰبِ الْحَكِيْمِ‏(1)\nALAAR TILKA AAYAATUL KETAABE HAKEEM.\nAlif, Lam, Ra. (A. L. R.) These are verses of the Book All-Wise.\nاَكَانَ لِلنَّاسِ عَجَبًا اَنْ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى رَجُلٍ مِّنْهُمْ اَنْ اَنْذِرِ النَّاسَ وَبَشِّرِ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اَنَّ لَهُمْ قَدَمَ صِدْقٍ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْؔؕ قَالَ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ اِنَّ هٰذَا لَسٰحِرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(2)\nAAKAANA LIN-NAASE A’AJABAN AN AAWHAYNAA ELAA RAJULIN MINHUM AN AANZERE NAASA WA BASH-SHERIL LAZEENA AAMANOO ANNAL LAHUM QADAMA SEDQIN I’NDAL RABBEHEM QAALA KAAFEROON INNAL HAAZAA LASAAHERUN MOBEEN.\nWhat! Is it for the people a wonder that We revealed unto a man from among themselves, saying “Warn thou! mankind and bear good tidings unto those who believe that there is a footing of firmness with their Lord;” (but) say the infidels “Verily this is an obvious sorcerer.\nاِنَّ رَبَّكُمُ اللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ فِىْ سِتَّةِ اَيَّامٍ ثُمَّ اسْتَوٰى عَلَى الْعَرْشِ يُدَبِّرُ الْاَمْرَؕ مَا مِنْ شَفِيْعٍ اِلَّا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ اِذْنِهٖ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمُ اللّٰهُ رَبُّكُمْ فَاعْبُدُوْهُ ؕ اَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(3)\nINNAL RABBAKOMUL LAAHO LAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA FEE SETTATE AYYAAMIN SUMMA TAWAA A’LAL A’RSHIL YUDABBERU AL-AAMRA MAA MIN SHAFEEA’IN ILLAA MIN BA’DE AEZNEH ZAA LEKUMU LAAHO RABBOKUM FAAA’BUDOOHU AFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nVerily, Your Lord is God Who created the heavens and the earth in six days (terms) and is firmly established on ‘Arsh ’ He regulateth everything; No intercessor can there be save after His leave; This is God, your Lord, Therefore Him (alone) worship ye; What! will ye not then mind?\nاِلَيْهِ مَرْجِعُكُمْ جَمِيْعًا ؕ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقًّا ؕ اِنَّهٗ يَبْدَؤُا الْخَلْقَ ثُمَّ يُعِيْدُهٗ لِيَجْزِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ بِالْقِسْطِؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَهُمْ شَرَابٌ مِّنْ حَمِيْمٍ وَّعَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌۢ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(4)\nELAYHE MARJE-O’KUM JAMEE-A’A WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQAN INNAHU YABDA-UL KHALQA SUMMA YO-E’EDOHU LE-YAJZEYAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE BIL-QESTE WAL LAZEENA KAFAROO LAHUM SHARAABUN MIN HAMEEMIN WWAA’AZAABUN ALEEM BEMAA KAANOO YAKFOROON.\nUnto Him shall return ye all; (this is) the promise of God in truth; Verily, (it is only) He (Who) beginneth the creation, then causeth it to return that He may with equity recompense those who believe and do good; and those who disbelieve, for them shall be the drink from the boiling fluids and a chastisement painful for they did disbelieve.\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ الشَّمْسَ ضِيَآءً وَّالْقَمَرَ نُوْرًا وَّقَدَّرَهٗ مَنَازِلَ لِتَعْلَمُوْا عَدَدَ السِّنِيْنَ وَالْحِسَابَؕ مَا خَلَقَ اللّٰهُ ذٰلِكَ اِلَّا بِالْحَقِّۚ يُفَصِّلُ الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَّعْلَمُوْنَ‏(5)\nHOWA LAZEE JA-A’LA SHAMSA ZEEAAAAN WWAALQAMARA NOORAN WWAQADDARAH MANAAZELA LE-TA’LAMOO A’ADADA AS-SENEENA WAL HESAABA MAA KHALAQAL LAAHO ZAALEKA ILLAA BIL-HAQQE YUFASSELU AAYAATE LE-QAWMIN-Y YA’LAMOON.\nHe is (the One) Who made the sun a radiation and the moon a light and planned into stations that ye might know the number of years and the reckoning (of time); created not God (all) this but for truth; (Thus) doth God make His signs manifest (clearly) for a people who know (Understand).\nاِنَّ فِى اخْتِلَافِ الَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ وَمَا خَلَقَ اللّٰهُ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّتَّقُوْنَ‏(6)\nINNAL FIL AKHTELAAFE LAYLE WAN NAHAARE WA MAA KHALAQAL LAAHO FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YYATTAQOONA.\nVerily in the variation of the night and the day, and what (all) hath created God in the heavens and in the earth, surely are there signs for a people who guard (themselves) against evil.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَرْجُوْنَ لِقَآءَنَا وَرَضُوْا بِالْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَاطْمَاَنُّوْا بِهَا وَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ عَنْ اٰيٰتِنَا غٰفِلُوْنَۙ‏(7)\nINNAL LAZEENA LAA YARJOON LEQAAANAA WARAZOOA BE-HAYAATID DUNYAA WAATMAANNOOA BEHAA WAL LAZEENA HUM A’N AAYAATENAA GHAAFELOON.\nVerily, those who hope not to meet Us (on the Day of Judgment) and are pleased with the life of this world and are satisfied with it, and those who are neglectful of Our signs.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ مَاْوٰٮهُمُ النَّارُ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(8)\nOOLAAA-EKA MAAWAAHUMU TAMASSANAN BEMAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nThese! their abode is the fire for what they did earn.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَ عَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ يَهْدِيْهِمْ رَبُّهُمْ بِاِيْمَانِهِمْۚ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهِمُ الْاَنْهٰرُ فِىْ جَنّٰتِ النَّعِيْمِ‏(9)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE YAHDEEHEM RABBOHUM BE-EEMAANEHIM TAJREE MIN TAHTEHEMU ANHAARO FEE JANNATIN NA-E’EM.\nVerily (for) those who believe and do good, guideth them their Lord by their faith, beneath them will flow rivers in gardens of bliss.\nدَعْوٰٮهُمْ فِيْهَا سُبْحٰنَكَ اللّٰهُمَّ وَ تَحِيَّتُهُمْ فِيْهَا سَلٰمٌۚ وَاٰخِرُ دَعْوٰٮهُمْ اَنِ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(10)\nDAA’WAAHUM FEEHAA SUBHAANAKA AL-LAAHUMMA WA TAHIYYATOHUM FEEHAA SALAAMUN WAAKHERU DAA’WAAHUM SAALEHAN HAMDO LILLAAHE RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nTheir cry therein (will be), “Glory be to Thee O’ God!” and their greetings in it (will be) ‘Peace’ and the last of their cry (will be), that God’s is the praise, the Lord of the worlds.\nوَلَوْ يُعَجِّلُ اللّٰهُ لِلنَّاسِ الشَّرَّ اسْتِعْجَالَهُمْ بِالْخَيْرِ لَقُضِىَ اِلَيْهِمْ اَجَلُهُمْؕ فَنَذَرُ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَرْجُوْنَ لِقَآءَنَا فِىْ طُغْيَانِهِمْ يَعْمَهُوْنَ‏(11)\nWA LAW YUA’AJJELU LAAHO LIN-NAASE ASH-SHARRA ASTEA’JAALAHUM BE-KHAYR LAQOZEYA ELAYHIM AAJALUHUM FANAZARU LAZEENA LAA YARJOON LEQAAANAA FEE TUGHYAANEHIM YA’MAHOON.\nAnd if God were to hasten unto men the evil (they have earned) as they would fain hasten on for (their) good, surely should have been decreed unto them their doom; But We leave those who hope not to meet Us (on the Day of Judgment) in their contumacy blindly wandering (bewildered).\nوَاِذَا مَسَّ الْاِنْسَانَ الضُّرُّ دَعَانَا لِجَنْۢبِهٖۤ اَوْ قَاعِدًا اَوْ قَآئِمًا ۚ فَلَمَّا كَشَفْنَا عَنْهُ ضُرَّهٗ مَرَّ كَاَنْ لَّمْ يَدْعُنَاۤ اِلٰى ضُرٍّ مَّسَّهٗؕ كَذٰلِكَ زُيِّنَ لِلْمُسْرِفِيْنَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(12)\nWA EZAA MASSAN INSAANA AZ-ZURRU DAA’AANAA LEJANBEH AW QAAE’EDAN AW QAAA-EMAA FALAMMAA KASHAFNAA A’NHO ZURRAH MARRA KA-AN LAM YADU’UNAA ELAA ZURRIN MMASSAH KAZAALEKA ZUYYENA LIL-MUSREFEENA MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nAnd when toucheth a man (an) affliction he crieth unto Us whether lying, or sitting or standing; but when remove We from him his affliction, he passes on as though he had not called unto Us an account of the affliction which did touch him; thus is made fairseeming unto the transgressors what they do.\nوَلَقَدْ اَهْلَكْنَا الْقُرُوْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ لَمَّا ظَلَمُوْا  ۙ وَجَآءَتْهُمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ وَمَا كَانُوْا لِيُؤْمِنُوْا  ؕ كَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْقَوْمَ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(13)\nWA LAQAD AHLAKNAL QOROONAL MIN QABLEKUM LAMMAA ZALAMOO WA JAAA-ATHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE WA MAA KAANOO LE-YOAMENOO KAZAALEKA NAJZIL QAWMAZ MUJREMEEN.\nAnd indeed We did destroy generations before you when they did wrong, and had come unto them apostles for them with clear signs but they would not believe; Thus do We recompense the guilty people.\nثُمَّ جَعَلْنٰكُمْ خَلٰٓئِفَ فِى الْاَرْضِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ لِنَنْظُرَ كَيْفَ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(14)\nSUMMA JA-A’LNAAKUM KHALAAAEFA FIL ARZE MIN BA’DEHIM LENANZURA KAYFA TA’MALOON.\nThen We made you (their) successors in the land after them, that We might see how ye act.\nوَاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيَاتُنَا بَيِّنٰتٍ ۙ قَالَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَرْجُوْنَ لِقَآءَنَا ائْتِ بِقُرْاٰنٍ غَيْرِ هٰذَاۤ اَوْ بَدِّلْهُ ؕ قُلْ مَا يَكُوْنُ لِىْۤ اَنْ اُبَدِّلَهٗ مِنْ تِلْقَآئِ نَفْسِىْ ۚ اِنْ اَتَّبِعُ اِلَّا مَا يُوْحٰۤى اِلَىَّ ۚ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اِنْ عَصَيْتُ رَبِّىْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(15)\nWA EZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHIM AAAYAATUNAA BAYYENAAT QAALA LAZEENA LAA YARJOON LEQAAANAA ATE BEQURAAANIN GHAIRE HAAZAA AW BADDELHU QUL MAA LAHUL LEE AN AUBADDELAH MIN TELQAAE NAFSEE IN AATTABEU’U ILLAA MAA YOOHAA ELAYYA INNEE AKHAAFO IN A’ASAYTU RABBEE A’ZAABAL YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nAnd when are recited unto them Our clear signs, those who hope not to meet Us say, “Bring thou a Qur’an other than this or change it;” say thou “it is not for me to change it as prompteth me; mine own self I follow naught but what is revealed unto me; Verily, I fear, if I disobey my Lord, the chastisement of a great day.\nقُلْ لَّوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ مَا تَلَوْتُهٗ عَلَيْكُمْ وَلَاۤ اَدْرٰٮكُمْ بِهٖ ۖ  فَقَدْ لَبِثْتُ فِيْكُمْ عُمُرًا مِّنْ قَبْلِهٖ ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(16)\nQUL LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO MAA TALAWTUH A’LAYKUM WA LAA AADRAAKUM BEHI FAQAD YAWMAN FEEKUM U’UMURAN MIN QABLEHI AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nSay thou, “If God hath so willed, I had not recited it unto you, nor would He have taught it to you; Indeed have I lived among you an age before it; What! then (yet) ye understand not?\nفَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا اَوْ كَذَّبَ بِاٰيٰتِهٖ ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُفْلِحُ الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ‏(17)\nFAMAN AZLAMO MIMMANIF TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN AW KAZZABA BE-AAYAATEHI INNAHU LAA YUFLEHUZ MUJREMOON.\nWho then doth more wrong than he who forgeth a lie against God or belieth His signs? Verily succeed not the guilty ones.\nوَيَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَضُرُّهُمْ وَلَا يَنْفَعُهُمْ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ شُفَعَآؤُنَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِؕ قُلْ اَتُنَبِّئُوْنَ اللّٰهَ بِمَا لَا يَعْلَمُ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَلَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ سُبْحٰنَهٗ وَتَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(18)\nWA YA’BODOON MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAA YAZURROHUM WA LAA YANFAU’UHUM WA YAQOOLOONA HAAOOLAAA-E SHUFAA’AAUNAA I’NDAL LAAH QUL AATUNABBEOONA LAAHA BEMAA LAA YA’LAMO FIL SAMAAWAATE WA LAA FIL ARZ WALADAN TA-A’ALAA A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nAnd worship they besides God, what can neither hurt them nor profit them, and say they: “These are our intercessors with God.” Say thou “What! (imagine) ye (to) inform God of what He knoweth not (of what is) in the heavens and in the earth?” Glory be to Him and Exalted is He (far) above what they associate (with Him).\nوَمَا كَانَ النَّاسُ اِلَّاۤ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً فَاخْتَلَفُوْا ؕ وَلَوْلَا كَلِمَةٌ سَبَقَتْ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ لَقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ فِيْمَا فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(19)\nWA MAA KAANA NAASO ILLAA UMMATAM WAAHEDATAN FA TALAFOO WA LAWLAA KALEMATUN SABAQAT MIN RABBEKA LAQOZEYA BAYNAHUM FEEMAA FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON.\nAnd mankind was naught but one community but (later) differed; and had not a word (of decree of respite) already gone forth from thy Lord, it would have been decided between them in respect of what they differ therein.\nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ اٰيَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖ ۚ فَقُلْ اِنَّمَا الْغَيْبُ لِلّٰهِ فَانْتَظِرُوْا ۚ اِنِّىْ مَعَكُمْ مِّنَ الْمُنْتَظِرِيْنَ‏(20)\nWA YAQOOLOONA LAWLAA UNZELA A’LAYHE TAA-TEENAA MIN RABBEHI FAQUL INNAMAA AL-GHAYBU LILLAAHE FAANTAZEROOA INNEE MA-A’KUM MENAL AL-MUNTAZEREENA.\nAnd they say, “Why is not a sign sent unto him from His lord?” Say thou “Verily the unseen is only for God, there-fore wait ye; verily I am (also) with you of the waiting ones.\nوَاِذَاۤ اَذَقْنَا النَّاسَ رَحْمَةً مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ ضَرَّآءَ مَسَّتْهُمْ اِذَا لَهُمْ مَّكْرٌ فِىْۤ اٰيَاتِنَا ؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُ اَسْرَعُ مَكْرًا ؕ اِنَّ رُسُلَنَا يَكْتُبُوْنَ مَا تَمْكُرُوْنَ‏(21)\nWA EZAA AZAQNAN NAASA RAHMATAM MIN BA’DE ZARAAA-A MASSATHUM EZAA LAHUM MMAKRUN FEE AAAYAATENAA QOLIL LAAHO AASRAU’U MAKRAWN INNAL RUSULANAA YAKTOBOONAL MAA TAMKUROONA.\nAnd when We make people taste of (Our) mercy after an affliction hath touched them; lo! they devise plots against Our signs; Say thou (O’ Our Apostle!) “God is quicker in devising; Verily Our messengers write down what (all) ye devise.\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُسَيِّرُكُمْ فِى الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِؕ حَتّٰۤى اِذَا كُنْتُمْ فِى الْفُلْكِ ۚ وَ جَرَيْنَ بِهِمْ بِرِيْحٍ طَيِّبَةٍ وَّفَرِحُوْا بِهَا جَآءَتْهَا رِيْحٌ عَاصِفٌ وَّجَآءَهُمُ الْمَوْجُ مِنْ كُلِّ مَكَانٍ وَّظَنُّوْۤا اَنَّهُمْ اُحِيْطَ بِهِمْ ۙ دَعَوُا اللّٰهَ مُخْلِصِيْنَ لَهُ الدِّيْنَۙ  لَئِنْ اَنْجَيْتَنَا مِنْ هٰذِهٖ لَنَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الشّٰكِرِيْنَ‏(22)\nHOWA LAZEE YUSAYRUKUM FIL BARRE WAL BAHRE HATTAA EZAA KUNTUM FIL FULKE WA JARAYNA BEHIM BEREEHIN TAYBATIN WWAFAREHOOA BEHAA JAAATHAA REEHUN A’AASEFUN WWAJAAAHUMU AL-MAWJU MIN KULLE MAKAANIN WWAZANNOOA ANNAHUM AUHEETA BEHIM DA-A’WUL LAAHA MUKHLESEENA LAHUL DEENA LAIL AANJAYTANAA MIN HAAZEHI LANAKOONANNA MENAL ASH-SHAAKEREENA.\nHe it is Who enableth you to travel by land and sea; so that ye go on board the ships; and they sail on with them in a favourable breeze, and they rejoice thereat, (and when cometh) unto them a violent gale and the billows surge in on them from all sides and they think that they are encompassed therewith, (then) they cry (praying) unto God, professing sincerity unto Him in (their) faith (in Him), saying: “If Thou (O’ Our Lord) dost deliver us from this, we shall indeed be of the grateful ones”.\nفَلَمَّاۤ اَنْجٰٮهُمْ اِذَا هُمْ يَبْغُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ ؕ يٰۤاَ يُّهَا النَّاسُ اِنَّمَا بَغْيُكُمْ عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِكُمْۙ مَّتَاعَ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ثُمَّ اِلَيْنَا مَرْجِعُكُمْ فَنُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(23)\nFALAMMAA AANJAAHUM EZAA HUM YABGHOONA FIL ARZE BEGHAYRIL HAQQE YAA A’ZAABAN AYYOHAL NAASO INNAMAA BAGHYUKUM A’LAA ANFOSEKUM MMATAAA’A HAYAATID DUNYAA SUMMA ELAYNAA MARJE-O’KUM FANUNABBEUKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nBut when He delivereth them, behold! they rebel in the earth unjustly; “O’ mankind! your rebellion is against your own selves, a provision for the life of (only) this world, then unto Us shall be your return, then will. We inform you of what ye were doing.\nاِنَّمَا مَثَلُ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا كَمَآءٍ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ فَاخْتَلَطَ بِهٖ نَبَاتُ الْاَرْضِ مِمَّا يَاْكُلُ النَّاسُ وَالْاَنْعَامُؕ حَتّٰۤى اِذَاۤ اَخَذَتِ الْاَرْضُ زُخْرُفَهَا وَازَّيَّنَتْ وَظَنَّ اَهْلُهَاۤ اَنَّهُمْ قٰدِرُوْنَ عَلَيْهَاۤ ۙ اَتٰٮهَاۤ اَمْرُنَا لَيْلًا اَوْ نَهَارًا فَجَعَلْنٰهَا حَصِيْدًا كَاَنْ لَّمْ تَغْنَ بِالْاَمْسِ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ نُفَصِّلُ الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَّتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(24)\nINNAMAA MASALUL HAYAATID DUNYAA KA-MAAA-IM ANZALNAAHO MENAL SAMAAA-E FAAKHTALATA BEHI NABAATU ARZE MIMMAA YAAKULU NAASO WAL AANA’AAMU HATTAA EZAA AAKHAZATE ARZO ZUKHRUFAHAA WAAZZAYNAT WA ZANNAS AAHLUHAA ANNAHUM QAADEROONA A’LAYHAA ATAAHAA AAMRUNAA LAYLAN AW NAHAARAN FA-JA-A’LNAAHAA HASEEDAN KA-AN LAM TAGHNA AMS KAZAALEKA NOFASSELUL AAYAATE LE-QAWMIN-Y YATAFAKKAROON.\nThe likeness of this world’s life is only as water which We send down from the sky; by its mingling grow the produce of the earth of which eat men and cattle; until when the earth puts on its golden raiment and gets garnished, and its people deem that they have power (of disposal) over it, (but suddenly) cometh Our command unto it, by night or by day, then We did render it as reaped, as though it had not existed yesterday; Thus do We explain the signs in details for people who reflect.\nوَاللّٰهُ يَدْعُوْۤا اِلٰى دَارِ السَّلٰمِؕ وَيَهْدِىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(25)\nWAL LAAHO YAD-O’O ELAA DAARE AS-SALAAME WA YAHDEE MAN YASHAAA-O ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nAnd God calleth (you) to the abode of peace; and guideth whomsoever He willeth unto the right way.\nلِلَّذِيْنَ اَحْسَنُوا الْحُسْنٰى وَزِيَادَةٌ ؕ وَلَا يَرْهَقُ وُجُوْهَهُمْ قَتَرٌ وَّلَا ذِلَّةٌ  ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَنَّةِ ۚ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(26)\nLILLAZEENA AAHSANOOA AL-HUSNAA WAZEEADATUN WA LAA YARHAQU WUJOOHAHUM QATARUN WA LAA ZELLATUN OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN JANNAH HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nFor those who do good is excellent reward and more (than this); No darkness shall cover their faces nor shall ignominy (befall them); these are the dwellers of the garden; in it shall they abide.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَسَبُوا السَّيِّاٰتِ جَزَآءُ سَيِّئَةٍ ۢ بِمِثْلِهَا ۙ وَتَرْهَقُهُمْ ذِلَّةٌ  ؕ مَا لَهُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ مِنْ عَاصِمٍ ۚ كَاَنَّمَاۤ اُغْشِيَتْ وُجُوْهُهُمْ قِطَعًا مِّنَ الَّيْلِ مُظْلِمًا ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِ ؕ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(27)\nWAL LAZEENA KASABOOA SAYYE-AATE JAZAAA-O SAYATIN BEMESLEHAA WATARHAQUHUM ZELLATUN MAA LAHUM MENAL LAAHE MIN A’AASEMIN KA-ANNAMAA AUGHSHEET WOJOOHOHUM QETAA’AN MENAL LAYLE MUZLEMAN OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN NAAR HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nAnd those who have earned evil, the recompense for evil is the like of it; and ignominy shall come upon them; from (the wrath of) God they shall have no protector; as if their faces have been covered as a piece of the darkening night; these are the inmates of the (Hell) fire; in it shall they abide.\nوَيَوْمَ نَحْشُرُهُمْ جَمِيْعًا ثُمَّ نَقُوْلُ لِلَّذِيْنَ اَشْرَكُوْا مَكَانَكُمْ اَنْتُمْ وَشُرَكَآؤُكُمْۚ فَزَيَّلْنَا بَيْنَهُمْ وَقَالَ شُرَكَآؤُهُمْ مَّا كُنْتُمْ اِيَّانَا تَعْبُدُوْنَ‏(28)\nWA YAWMA NAHSHURUHUM JAMEE-A’A SUMMA NAQOOLU LILLAZEENA ASHRAKOO MAKAANAKUM ANTUM WASHURAKAAUKUM FAZAYLNAA BAYNAHUM WA QAALA SHURAKAAUHUM MAA KUNTUM IYYAANAA TA’BODOONA.\nOn the day (of resurrection) when We will gather them all together, then will We say unto those who associated others (with Us) “Keep ye where ye are, ye and your associated gods;” then We shall separate them, the one from the other, and shall say (unto them) their associate gods “It was not us that ye worshipped ”.\nفَكَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ شَهِيْدًۢا بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكُمْ اِنْ كُنَّا عَنْ عِبَادَتِكُمْ لَغٰفِلِيْنَ‏(29)\nFA KAFAA BIL-LAAHE SHAHEEDAA BAYNANAA WA BAYNAKUM IN KUNNAA A’N E’EBAADATEKUM LAGHAAFELEENA.\nTherefore, God is a sufficient witness between us and you (that) we certainly, of your worship (of us), were unaware.\nهُنَالِكَ تَبْلُوْا كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّاۤ اَسْلَفَتْ وَرُدُّوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ مَوْلٰٮهُمُ الْحَقِّ وَضَلَّ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(30)\nHONAALEKAB TABLOOA KULLO NAFSIM MAA AASLAFAT WARUDDOOA ELAL LAAHE MAWLAAHUMU HAQQE WA ZALLA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nThere shall every soul realize what it hath sent before, and they shall be brought back to God, their true Lord, and what they did fabricate (the false deities) will vanish (away) from them.\nقُلْ مَنْ يَّرْزُقُكُمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ اَمَّنْ يَّمْلِكُ السَّمْعَ وَالْاَبْصَارَ وَ مَنْ يُّخْرِجُ الْحَىَّ مِنَ الْمَيِّتِ وَيُخْرِجُ الْمَيِّتَ مِنَ الْحَىِّ وَمَنْ يُّدَبِّرُ الْاَمْرَؕ فَسَيَقُوْلُوْنَ اللّٰهُۚ فَقُلْ اَفَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(31)\nQUL MAN YARZOQOKUM MENAL SAMAAA-E WAL ARZE AMMAN FAMANY JA-A’LA LAKOMUS SAM-A’ WA MAN YYUKHREJU HAYYA MENAL MAYYETE WA YUKHREJUL MAYYETA MENAL HAYYE WA MAN YYUDABBERU AL-AAMRA FASAYAQOOLOONA LAAHO FAQUL AFALAA TATTAQOON.\nSay (thou O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Who provideth you sustenance from the sky and from the earth? or who controlled! the hearing and the sight? and who bringeth forth the living from the dead, and bringeth forth the dead from the living? and who administreth (every) affair?” Then they will say “God”. Then say (thou unto them) “Will ye not then guard (yourselves against His displeasure)?\nفَذٰلِكُمُ اللّٰهُ رَبُّكُمُ الْحَقُّ  ۚ فَمَاذَا بَعْدَ الْحَقِّ اِلَّا الضَّلٰلُ ۚ فَاَنّٰى تُصْرَفُوْنَ‏(32)\nFAZAALEKUMU LAAHO RABBUKUMU HAQQO FA MAA BA’DA HAQQE ILLAA AZ-ZALAALU FA-ANNAA TUSRAFOONA.\nThen this is God, your true Lord; and what is apart from truth but error; whereto then are ye turned away?\nكَذٰلِكَ حَقَّتْ كَلِمَتُ رَبِّكَ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ فَسَقُوْۤا اَنَّهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(33)\nKAZAALEKA HAQQAT KALEMATU RABBEKA A’LAL LAZEENA FASAQOOA ANNAHUM LAA YOAMENOONA.\nThus is proved true the word of thy Lord against those who transgress that they believe not.\nقُلْ هَلْ مِنْ شُرَكَآئِكُمْ مَّنْ يَّبْدَؤُا الْخَلْقَ ثُمَّ يُعِيْدُهٗ ؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُ يَبْدَؤُا الْخَلْقَ ثُمَّ يُعِيْدُهٗؕ فَاَنّٰى تُؤْفَكُوْنَ‏(34)\nQUL HAL MIN SHURAKAAEKUM MAN YABDAUL KHALQA SUMMA YO-E’EDOHU QOLIL LAAHO YABDA-UL KHALQA SUMMA YUE’EEDUH FA-ANNAA TUFAKOONA.\nSay (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Of your associates, is there anyone who can originate the creation (and), then return it?” Say thou! “God alone doth originate the creation and returneth it whereunto are ye then inclined away?\nقُلْ هَلْ مِنْ شُرَكَآئِكُمْ مَّنْ يَّهْدِىْۤ اِلَى الْحَقِّؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُ يَهْدِىْ لِلْحَقِّؕ اَفَمَنْ يَّهْدِىْۤ اِلَى الْحَقِّ اَحَقُّ اَنْ يُّتَّبَعَ اَمَّنْ لَّا يَهِدِّىْۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يُّهْدٰىۚ فَمَا لَكُمْ كَيْفَ تَحْكُمُوْنَ‏(35)\nQUL HAL MIN SHURAKAAEKUM MAN YAHDEE ELAL HAQQ QOLIL LAAHO YAHDEE LIL-HAQQE AFAMAWN YAHDEE ELAL HAQQE AHAQQO AN YYUTTABAA’A AMMAN LAA YAHEDDEAA ILLAA AN YYUHDAA FAMAA LAKUM KAYFA TAHKUMOONA.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “Of your associates is there anyone who can guide unto truth?” Say thou! “It is God alone Who guideth unto truth; Is then He Who guideth unto truth more worthy to be followed or he who himself goeth not aright unless he is guided? What then hath be-fallen you? How (ill) ye judge?\nوَمَا يَتَّبِعُ اَكْثَرُهُمْ اِلَّا ظَنًّا ؕاِنَّ الظَّنَّ لَا يُغْنِىْ مِنَ الْحَقِّ شَيْئًا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِمَا يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(36)\nWA MAA YATTABEU’U AKSAROHUM ILLAA ZANNAN AENNA AZ-ZANNA LAA YUGHNEE MENAL HAQQE SHAY-ANW INNAL LAAHA A’LEEM BEMAA YAF-A’LOON.\nAnd follow not most of them (anything) but (their own) conjecture; verily conjecture cannot avail anything against the truth; verily God knoweth all what they do.\nوَمَا كَانَ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنُ اَنْ يُّفْتَرٰى مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَلٰكِنْ تَصْدِيْقَ الَّذِىْ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ وَتَفْصِيْلَ الْكِتٰبِ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهِ مِنْ رَّبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(37)\nWA MAA KAANA HAAZAA QUR-AANO AN YYUFTARAA MIN DOONIL LAAHE WA LAAKIL TASDEEQA LAZEE BAYNA YADAYHE WATAFSEELA KETAABE LAA RAYBA FEEHE MIN RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd this Qur’an is not such as to be forged by (any one) besides God, but it is a confirmation of (the scriptures) that went before it and (the clearest) explanation of the Book, there is no doubt in it, (it is) from the Lord of the worlds.\nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ افْتَرٰٮهُ ؕ قُلْ فَاْتُوْا بِسُوْرَةٍ مِّثْلِهٖ وَادْعُوْا مَنِ اسْتَطَعْتُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(38)\nAM YAQOOLOONA AFTARAAHU QUL FAATOO BE-SOORATIM MISLEH WAD-O’O MANIS ENIS TA-TA’TUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nOr do they say: “He (Apostle Muhammad) hath forged it?” Say thou! “Bring ye then a chapter like unto it and call on (to your aid) whomsoever ye can, besides God, if ye be truthful.\nبَلْ كَذَّبُوْا بِمَا لَمْ يُحِيْطُوْا بِعِلْمِهٖ وَلَمَّا يَاْتِهِمْ تَاْوِيْلُهٗ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ كَذَّبَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ فَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(39)\nBAL KAZZABOO BEMAA LAM YUHEETOOA BE-I’LMEHI WA LAMMAA YAATEHEM TAAWEELUH KAZAALEKA KAZZABA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM FANZUR KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL ZAALEMEEN.\nNay, they belied that which they comprehended not with the knowledge of it and the explanation of it came not unto them; even thus did belie those before them, see then what was the end of the unjust ones.\nوَ مِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يُّؤْمِنُ بِهٖ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ لَّا يُؤْمِنُ بِهٖؕ وَرَبُّكَ اَعْلَمُ بِالْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(40)\nWA MINHUM MAN YOAMENO BEHI WA MINHUM MAN LAA BIL LAAHE BEH WA RABBOKA A-A’LAMO BE-MUFSEDEEN.\nAnd of them is he who believeth in it, and of them is he who believeth not in it; and thy Lord knoweth best the mischief-makers.\nوَاِنْ كَذَّبُوْكَ فَقُلْ لِّىْ عَمَلِىْ وَلَكُمْ عَمَلُكُمْۚ اَنْتُمْ بَرِيْٓئُوْنَ مِمَّاۤ اَعْمَلُ وَاَنَا بَرِىْٓءٌ مِّمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(41)\nWA KAZZABOOKA FAQUL LEE A’AMALEAA WA LAKUM A’AMALUKUM ANTUM BAREEOONA MIMMAA AAA’MALU ANAT BAREEE-UM MIMMAA TA’MALOON.\nAnd if they belie thee, say thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “For me is my work and for you is your work, ye are clear oft’ of what I do and I am clear off of what ye do.\nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّسْتَمِعُوْنَ اِلَيْكَؕ اَفَاَنْتَ تُسْمِعُ الصُّمَّ وَلَوْ كَانُوْا لَا يَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(42)\nWA MINHUM MAN YYASTAMEU’OONA AELAYKA AAFAANTA TUSME-U’S SUMMAD WA LAW KAANOO LAA YA’QELOON.\nAnd of them are those who hearken unto thee; canst thou make the deaf hear? though they understand not.\nوَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّنْظُرُ اِلَيْكَ ؕ اَفَاَنْتَ تَهْدِى الْعُمْىَ وَ لَوْ كَانُوْا لَا يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(43)\nWA MINHUM MAN YYANZURU ELAYKA AAFAANTA TAHDEAA AL-U’UMAAA WA LAW KAANOO LAA YUBSEROON.\nAnd of them are those who look at thee; canst thou guide the blind though they see not.\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَظْلِمُ النَّاسَ شَيْئًا وَّلٰكِنَّ النَّاسَ اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(44)\nINNAL LAAHA LAA YAZLEMU NAASA SHAY-ANW WA LAAKINNA NAASA ANFOSAHUM YAZLEMOON.\nVerily, God doeth not any injustice to people, but men to their (own) selves do injustice.\nوَيَوْمَ يَحْشُرُهُمْ كَاَنْ لَّمْ يَلْبَثُوْۤا اِلَّا سَاعَةً مِّنَ النَّهَارِ يَتَعَارَفُوْنَ بَيْنَهُمْؕ قَدْ خَسِرَ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِلِقَآءِ اللّٰهِ وَمَا كَانُوْا مُهْتَدِيْنَ‏(45)\nWA YAWMA YAHSHURUHUM KA-AN LAM YALBASOOA ILLAA SAAA’ATAN MENAL AN-NAHAARE YATAA’AARAFOONA BAYNAHUM QAD KHASERA LAZEENA KAZZABOO BELEQAAE LAAHE WA MAA KAANOO MOHTADEEN.\nAnd on the day (of resurrection) when He will gather them as though they had not tarried in the world or in the grave but an hour of the day, they will recognise each other; Indeed will perish those who belied the meeting with God and were not guided aright.\nوَاِمَّا نُرِيَنَّكَ بَعْضَ الَّذِىْ نَعِدُهُمْ اَوْ نَتَوَفَّيَنَّكَ فَاِلَيْنَا مَرْجِعُهُمْ ثُمَّ اللّٰهُ شَهِيْدٌ عَلٰى مَا يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(46)\nWA AMMAA NUREENNAKA YAWM LAZEE NAE’EDUHUM AW NATAWAFFAYANNAKA FA ELAYNAA MARJEU’UHUM SUMMA LAAHO WA A’LAA MAA YAF-A’LOON.\nAnd if We let thee behold something of (Our wrath) what We warn them against or (before that) We take thee to Ourselves, (even) then unto Us is their return, then God is a witness to (all) what they do.\nوَلِكُلِّ اُمَّةٍ رَّسُوْلٌ ۚ فَاِذَا جَآءَ رَسُوْلُهُمْ قُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ بِالْقِسْطِ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(47)\nWA LEKULLIM UMMATIN RRASOOLUN FA-EZAA JAAA-A RASOOLUHUM QUZEAAA BAYNAHUM BIL QISTE WA HUM LAA LAA YUZLAMOON.\nAnd for every people (was sent) an apostle; and when came their apostle, the matter between them was decided with equity and they shall not (in the least) be done (any) injustice.\nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَتٰى هٰذَا الْوَعْدُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(48)\nWA YAQOOLOONA MATAA HAAZAA WA’DO IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nAnd say they “When this promise (of Our wrath) will come to pass, if ye be truthful.\nقُلْ لَّاۤ اَمْلِكُ لِنَفْسِىْ ضَرًّا وَّلَا نَفْعًا اِلَّا مَا شَآءَ اللّٰهُؕ لِكُلِّ اُمَّةٍ اَجَلٌؕ اِذَا جَآءَ اَجَلُهُمْ فَلَا يَسْتَاخِرُوْنَ سَاعَةً وَّلَا يَسْتَقْدِمُوْنَ‏(49)\nQUL LAA AAMLEKU LE-NAFSEE BEKUM WA LAA BEKUM ILLAA MAA SHAAA-ALLAAH LEKULLIM UMMATIN AAJALUN EZAA JAAA-A AAJALUHUM FALAA YASTAAKHEROONA SAAA’ATAN WA LAA YASTAQDEMOONA.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle!) “I own not for myself any harm nor any benefit save what willeth God; To every people is an appointed term; when cometh their term then shall they neither retard (even) an hour nor go before it.\nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ اَتٰٮكُمْ عَذَابُهٗ بَيَاتًا اَوْ نَهَارًا مَّاذَا يَسْتَعْجِلُ مِنْهُ الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ‏(50)\nQUL ARA-AYTUM IN AATAAKUM A’AZAABUH BAYAATAN AW NAHAARAN MMAAZAA YASTAA’JELU MINHO MUJREMOON.\nSay thou (O’ Muhammad!) “Do ye see if His chastisement cometh upon you by night or by day, what then is there of it that the guilty hasten for?\nاَثُمَّ اِذَا مَا وَقَعَ اٰمَنْتُمْ بِهٖؕ اٰۤلْٴٰنَ وَقَدْ كُنْتُمْ بِهٖ تَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ‏(51)\nAASUMMA EZAA MAA WAQA-A’L AAMANTUM BEH AAALNA WA QAD KUNTUM BEHI TAS-TA’JELOONA.\nIs it when it cometh to pass, ye will believe in it? What! now (believe ye)? when ye have been (challenging in it and) hastening it on?\nثُمَّ قِيْلَ لِلَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا ذُوْقُوْا عَذَابَ الْخُلْدِۚ هَلْ تُجْزَوْنَ اِلَّا بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(52)\nSUMMA QEELA LILLAZEENA ZALAMOO ZOOQOO A’ZAABAL AL-KHULDE HAL TUJZAWNA ILLAA BEMAA KUNTUM TAKSEBOONA.\nThen shall it be said unto those who had been unjust: “Taste ye abiding punishment! Would ye (then) receive other than what ye have wrought?\nوَيَسْتَنْۢبِئُوْنَكَ اَحَقٌّ هُوَ ؕؔ قُلْ اِىْ وَرَبِّىْۤ اِنَّهٗ لَحَقٌّ ؔؕ وَمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ بِمُعْجِزِيْنَ‏(53)\nWAYASTANBEOONAKA AAHAQQUN HOWA QUL AEAA WA RABBEE INNAHU LAHAQQUN WA MAA ANTUM BE-MO’JEZEENA.\nAnd they ask thee: “Is that true?” Say thou! “Aye! By my Lord! Verily, Verily, it is the truth; and ye will not escape (His wrath).\nوَلَوْ اَنَّ لِكُلِّ نَفْسٍ ظَلَمَتْ مَا فِى الْاَرْضِ لَافْتَدَتْ بِهٖؕ وَاَسَرُّوا النَّدَامَةَ لَمَّا رَاَوُا الْعَذَابَۚ وَقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ بِالْقِسْطِ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(54)\nWA LAW ANNAL LEKULLIM NAFSIM ZALAMAT MAA FIL ARZE LAAFTADAT BEH WAASARROOA AN-NADAAMATA LAMMAA RAAWUA A’ZAABA WA BAYNAHUM BIL QISTE WA HUM LAA LAA YUZLAMOON.\nAnd if every soul that hath done injustice had all that is in the earth, it would assuredly ransom itself therewith; and they will proclaim their repentance when they behold the doom, and it shall be decided between them with justice and they shall not be done (any) injustice.\nاَلَاۤ اِنَّ لِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّ وَّلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(55)\nALAA INNAL LILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ ALAA INNAL WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQUWN WA LAAKINNA AKSARAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nBe it known verily God’s is what is in the heavens and the earth; Be it (also) known, Verily, God’s promise is true, but most of them know not.\nهُوَ يُحْىٖ وَيُمِيْتُ وَاِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(56)\nHOWA YOHYEE WA YOMEETO WA ELAYHE TURJA-O’ON.\nHe giveth life and causeth to die, and unto Him (Alone) shall ye (all) return.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ قَدْ جَآءَتْكُمْ مَّوْعِظَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَشِفَآءٌ لِّمَا فِى الصُّدُوْرِۙ  وَهُدًى وَّرَحْمَةٌ لِّلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(57)\nYAA AYYOHAL NAASO QAD JAAA-ATKUM MMAWE’EZATUN MIN RABBEKUM WA LEMAA FIL SODOOR WA HODANW WA RAHMATUL LIL-MOAMENEEN.\nO’ mankind! Indeed hath come unto you an exhortation from your Lord, and a cure for (the diseases) what is in your breasts and a guidance and mercy for the believers.\nقُلْ بِفَضْلِ اللّٰهِ وَبِرَحْمَتِهٖ فَبِذٰلِكَ فَلْيَفْرَحُوْا ؕ هُوَ خَيْرٌ مِّمَّا يَجْمَعُوْنَ‏(58)\nQUL BE-FAZLIL LAAHE WA BE-RAHMATEHI FABEZAALEKA FALYAFRAHOOA HOWA KHAYRUL MIMMAA YAJMAU’OONA.\nSay! (that) in the grace of God and in His mercy, in that they should rejoice; it is better than (the wealth) that they gather.\nقُلْ اَرَءَيْتُمْ مَّاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ مِّنْ رِّزْقٍ فَجَعَلْتُمْ مِّنْهُ حَرَامًا وَّحَلٰلًا ؕ قُلْ آٰللّٰهُ اَذِنَ لَكُمْ اَمْ عَلَى اللّٰهِ تَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(59)\nQUL ARA-AYTUM MAA ANZALAL LAAHO LAKUM MIN RREZQIN FAJAA’ALTUM MINHO HARAAMAN WWAHALAALAN QUL AAAALLLAAHU AZENA LAKUM AM A’LAL LAAHE TAFTAROONA.\nSay thou! “See ye what (things) God hath sent down for you of sustenance, then ye made something of it unlawful and (something of it) lawful.” Say thou! “Hath God permitted you or ye forge a lie against God?\nوَمَا ظَنُّ الَّذِيْنَ يَفْتَرُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ الْكَذِبَ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَذُوْ فَضْلٍ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(60)\nWA MAA ZANNU LAZEENA YAFTAROON A’LAL LAAHE AL-KAZEBA YAWMA AL-QEEMATE INNAL LAAHA LAZOO FAZLIN A’LAL NAASE LAAKINNAL AKSARAHUM LAA YASHKOROON.\nAnd what imagine those who forge lies against God on the Day of Resurrection? Verily, God is the Lord of grace for mankind, but most of them thank not.\nوَمَا تَكُوْنُ فِىْ شَاْنٍ وَّمَا تَتْلُوْا مِنْهُ مِنْ قُرْاٰنٍ وَّلَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ مِنْ عَمَلٍ اِلَّا كُنَّا عَلَيْكُمْ شُهُوْدًا اِذْ تُفِيْضُوْنَ فِيْهِؕ وَمَا يَعْزُبُ عَنْ رَّبِّكَ مِنْ مِّثْقَالِ ذَرَّةٍ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَا فِى السَّمَآءِ وَلَاۤ اَصْغَرَ مِنْ ذٰ لِكَ وَلَاۤ اَكْبَرَ اِلَّا فِىْ كِتٰبٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(61)\nWA MAA TAKOONO FEE SHAAN WA MAA TATLOO MINHO MIN QURAAANIN WA LAA TA’MALOON MIN A’AMALIN ILLAA KUNNAA A’LAYKUM SHUHOODAN IZ TUFEEZOONA FEEH WA MAA YAA’ZUBU A’N RABBEKA MIN MMESQAALE ZARRATIN FIL ARZE WA LAA FIL SAMAAA-E WA LAA AASGHARA MIN ZAA LEKA WA LAA AAKBARA ILLAA FEE KETAABIM MOBEEN.\nAnd thou art not (engaged) in any affair, nor dost thou recite any part of the (Holy) Qur’an and nor any deed ye (mankind) be doing, but We are witness over you when ye are engrossed therein; And doth not lie concealed from thy Lord (even) the weight of an atom in the earth nor in the heaven, nor anything lesser than that nor greater but it is (recorded) in a clear book.\nاَلَاۤ اِنَّ اَوْلِيَآءَ اللّٰهِ لَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَ ۖ ۚ‏(62)\nALAA INNAL AAWLEEAAAA LAAHE LAA KHAWFUN A’LAYHIM WA LAA HUM HUM YAHZANOON.\nBe it known, verily, the friends of God, no fear shall be on them, nor do they grieve.\nالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَكَانُوْا يَتَّقُوْنَؕ‏(63)\nLAZEENA AAMANOO WA KAANOO YATTAQOONA.\nThose who believe and guarded (themselves) against evil.\nلَهُمُ الْبُشْرٰى فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَفِى الْاٰخِرَةِؕ لَا تَبْدِيْلَ لِكَلِمٰتِ اللّٰهِؕ ذٰلِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيْمُؕ‏(64)\nLAHOMUL AL-BUSHRAA FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA WA AL-AAAKHERATE LAA TABDEELA LEKALEMAATE LAAH ZAALEKA HOWA FAWZUL AL-A’AZEEMU.\nFor them are glad tidings in the life in this world and in the hereafter; there is no changing the words of God; that is the great achievement.\nوَلَا يَحْزُنْكَ قَوْلُهُمْۘ اِنَّ الْعِزَّةَ لِلّٰهِ جَمِيْعًا ؕ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(65)\nWA LAA YAHZUNKA QAWLOHUM INNAL AL-E’EZZATA LILLAAHE JAMEE-A’A HOWA SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nAnd let not their discourse grieve thee, Verily, glory is wholly God’s; He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.\nاَلَاۤ اِنَّ لِلّٰهِ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِؕ وَمَا يَتَّبِعُ الَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ شُرَكَآءَ ؕ اِنْ يَّتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا الظَّنَّ وَاِنْ هُمْ اِلَّا يَخْرُصُوْنَ‏(66)\nALAA INNAL LILLAAHE MAN FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAN FIL ARZ WA MAA YATTABEU’U LAZEENA YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE SHORA-KAAA-A IN YYATTABEU’OONA ILLAA AZ-ZANNA WA HUM ILLAA YAKHRUSOONA.\nBe it known, Verily, God’s is whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth; They (really) follow not any associates (of God), who call on others besides God; they follow not anything but (their own) gesture, and they only lie.\nهُوَ الَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الَّيْلَ لِتَسْكُنُوْا فِيْهِ وَالنَّهَارَ مُبْصِرًا ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّسْمَعُوْنَ‏(67)\nHOWA LAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL LAYLA LETASKONOO FEEHE WAN NAHAARA MUBSERAN INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YASMA-O’ON.\nHe it is who did make for you the night that ye might rest in it, and the sight-giving day; Verily there are signs in it for people who hearken.\nقَالُوْا اتَّخَذَ اللّٰهُ وَلَدًا سُبْحٰنَهٗ ؕ هُوَ الْغَنِىُّ ؕ لَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ ؕ اِنْ عِنْدَكُمْ مِّنْ سُلْطٰنٍۢ بِهٰذَا ؕ اَتَقُوْلُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(68)\nQAALOO TAKHAZA LAAHO LAAHO WALADAN HOWA AL-GHANEAAAU LAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE IN E’ENDAKUM MIN SULTAANIN BEHAAZAA AATAQOOLOONA A’LAL LAAHE MAA LAA TA’LAMOON.\nSay they: God hath taken a son (unto Himself!) Glory be to Him! He is the Self-Sufficient; His (exclusively) is whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth; ye have no authority for this; What! say ye against God what ye know not?\nقُلْ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَفْتَرُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ الْكَذِبَ لَا يُفْلِحُوْنَؕ‏(69)\nQUL INNAL LAZEENA YAFTAROON A’LAL LAAHE AL-KAZEBA LAA YUFLEHOONA.\nSay thou, Verily those who forge a lie against God succeed not.\nمَتَاعٌ فِى الدُّنْيَا ثُمَّ اِلَيْنَا مَرْجِعُهُمْ ثُمَّ نُذِيْقُهُمُ الْعَذَابَ الشَّدِيْدَ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(70)\nLIL-MOTAALLAQAATE FIL DUNYAA SUMMA ELAYNAA MARJEU’UHUM SUMMA NUZEEQUHUMU A’ZAABA ASH-SHADEEDA BEMAA KAANOO YAKFOROON.\nA provision (it is only) in this world, then unto Us (only) is their return, then shall We make them taste severe chastisement for what they did disbelieve.\nوَاتْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ نَبَاَ نُوْحٍۘ اِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهٖ يٰقَوْمِ اِنْ كَانَ كَبُرَ عَلَيْكُمْ مَّقَامِىْ وَتَذْكِيْرِىْ بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ فَعَلَى اللّٰهِ تَوَكَّلْتُ فَاَجْمِعُوْۤا اَمْرَكُمْ وَشُرَكَآءَكُمْ ثُمَّ لَا يَكُنْ اَمْرُكُمْ عَلَيْكُمْ غُمَّةً ثُمَّ اقْضُوْۤا اِلَىَّ وَ لَا تُنْظِرُوْنِ‏(71)\nWAATLU A’LAYHIM NABAA NOOHIN IZ QAALA LEQAWMEHI LE-QAWMEHI IN KAANA KABURA A’LAYKUM MMAQAAMEAA WATAZKEEREAA BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE FA A’LAL LAAHE TAWAKKALTU FAAJMEU’OOA AAMRAKUM WA SHORAKAAA-AKUM SUMMA LAA YAKUL AAMRUKUM A’LAYKUM GHUMMATAN SUMMA AQZOOA ELAYYA WA LAA TUNZEROONE.\nAnd recite unto them the story of Noah when said he to his people: “O’ my people! if my stay and my reminding (you) of the signs of God be hard on you yet on God do I rely, muster therefore your designs and (gather) your associates (false gods), then let not your designs be dubious, then execute on me and give no respite (to me).\nفَاِنْ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ فَمَا سَاَلْتُكُمْ مِّنْ اَجْرٍؕاِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلَى اللّٰهِۙ وَاُمِرْتُ اَنْ اَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(72)\nFA-IN TAWALLAYTUM FAMAA SAALTUKUM MIN AAJRINAEN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAL LAAHE WA AN A-A’BODA AN SHAY-IWN WA MENAL AKOONA MENAL MUSLEMEEN.\nBut if ye turn back, (remember ye) then asked I not any recompense from you; my recompense is only (expected) from God, and I am commanded to be of those submitted unto God (Muslims).\nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَنَجَّيْنٰهُ وَمَنْ مَّعَهٗ فِى الْفُلْكِ وَجَعَلْنٰهُمْ خَلٰٓئِفَ وَاَغْرَقْنَا الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا ۚ فَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُنْذَرِيْنَ‏(73)\nFA-KAZZABOOHO FANAJJAYNAAHU WA MAN MMAA’AH FIL FULKE WA JA-A’LNAAHUM KHALAAAEFA WAAGHRAQNAA LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA FANZUR KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MUNZEREEN.\nBut they belied him so We delivered him and those with him in the Ark, and We made them successors and drowned those who belied Our signs; see then what was the end of the warned ones!\nثُمَّ بَعَثْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ رُسُلًا اِلٰى قَوْمِهِمْ فَجَآءُوْهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَمَا كَانُوْا لِيُؤْمِنُوْا بِمَا كَذَّبُوْا بِهٖ مِنْ قَبْلُ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ نَطْبَعُ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِ الْمُعْتَدِيْنَ‏(74)\nSUMMA BAA’ASNAA MIN BA’DEHI ROSOLAN ELAA QAWMEHIM FA-JAAA-OOHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE FAMAA KAANOO LE-YOAMENOO BEMAA KAZZABOO BEHI MIN QABLO KAZAALEKA NATBAU’U A’LAA QOLOOBIL MO’TADEEN.\nThen We did raise up after him apostles unto their people, so they came unto them with clear evidences but they would not believe in what they had belied before; Thus do We seal up the hearts of the transgressors!\nثُمَّ بَعَثْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ مُّوْسٰى وَهٰرُوْنَ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَاِ۫ ئِهٖ بِاٰيٰتِنَا فَاسْتَكْبَرُوْا وَكَانُوْا قَوْمًا مُّجْرِمِيْنَ‏(75)\nSUMMA BAA’ASNAA MIN BA’DEHIM MOOSAA WA AALO ELAA FIR-A’WNA WAMALAA EH BE-AAYAATENAA FAS-TAKBAROO WA KAANOO QAWMAN MMUJREMEENA.\nThen We did send after them Moses and Aaron to Pharaoh and his chiefs with Our signs (miracles) but they showed arrogance and they were a guilty people.\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ عِنْدِنَا قَالُوْۤا اِنَّ هٰذَا لَسِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(76)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AHOMUL HAQQO MIN I’NDENAA QAALOO INNAL HAAZAA LASEHRUN MOBEEN.\nAnd so when the truth came unto them from Us said they: “Verily, this is clear sorcery.\nقَالَ مُوْسٰٓى اَتَقُوْلُوْنَ لِلْحَقِّ لَمَّا جَآءَكُمْ ؕ اَسِحْرٌ هٰذَا ؕ وَلَا يُفْلِحُ السَّاحِرُوْنَ‏(77)\nQAALA MOOSAA AATAQOOLOONA LIL-HAQQE LAMMAA JAAA-AKUM AASEHRUN HAAZAA WA LAA YUFLEHUZ AS-SAAHEROONA.\nSaid Moses: “What! say ye (this) of the truth when it hath come unto you? Is this sorcery? And sorcerers succeed not.\nقَالُوْۤا اَجِئْتَنَا لِتَلْفِتَنَا عَمَّا وَجَدْنَا عَلَيْهِ اٰبَآءَنَا وَتَكُوْنَ لَكُمَا الْكِبْرِيَآءُ فِى الْاَرْضِؕ وَمَا نَحْنُ لَكُمَا بِمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(78)\nQAALOO AAJETANAA LETALFETANAA A’MMAA WAJADNAA A’LAYHE AABAAA-ANAA WA TAKOONA LAKOMAA AL-KEBREEAAAU FIL ARZ WA MAA NAHNO LAKOMAA BE-MOAMENEEN.\nSaid they: “Hast thou come to us to turn us away from (the faith) what we found our fathers upon, and that for ye two (only) may be the greatness in the land? And in ye two we are not believers.\nوَقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ ائْتُوْنِىْ بِكُلِّ سٰحِرٍ عَلِيْمٍ‏(79)\nWA QAALA FIRA’WNO ATOONEAA BEKULLE SAAHERIN A’LEEM.\nSaid Pharaoh: “Bring unto me every sorcerer (thoroughly) skilled.\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَ السَّحَرَةُ قَالَ لَهُمْ مُّوْسٰۤى اَلْقُوْا مَاۤ اَنْتُمْ مُّلْقُوْنَ‏(80)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-A AS-SAHARATU QAALA LAHUM MOOSAA AALQOOA MAA ANTUM MMULQOONA.\nWhen came the sorcerers, said unto them Moses: “Cast ye down what ye have to cast.\nفَلَمَّاۤ اَلْقَوْا قَالَ مُوْسٰى مَا جِئْتُمْ بِهِۙ السِّحْرُؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَيُبْطِلُهٗ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُصْلِحُ عَمَلَ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(81)\nFALAMMAA AALQAWA QAALA MOOSAA MAA JETUM BEHIL AS-SEHRU INNAL LAAHA SAYUBTELUH INNAL LAAHA LAA YUSLEHU A’AMALA MUFSEDEEN.\nSo when they had cast down (their rods and cords) said Moses (unto them) “what ye have brought of sorcery; Verily God will presently make it naught; Verily, God causeth not to thrive the work of the mischief- makers.\nوَيُحِقُّ اللّٰهُ الْحَقَّ بِكَلِمٰتِهٖ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ‏(82)\nWAYUHEQQU LAAHO HAQQA BEKALEMAATEH WA LAW KAREHA MUJREMOON.\nAnd God will prove the truth to be the truth by His words, though the guilty ones be averse (to it).\nفَمَاۤ اٰمَنَ لِمُوْسٰٓى اِلَّا ذُرِّيَّةٌ مِّنْ قَوْمِهٖ عَلٰى خَوْفٍ مِّنْ فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَا۟ ئِهِمْ اَنْ يَّفْتِنَهُمْ ؕ وَاِنَّ فِرْعَوْنَ لَعَالٍ فِى الْاَرْضِ ۚ وَاِنَّهٗ لَمِنَ الْمُسْرِفِيْنَ‏(83)\nFAMAA AAMANA LE-MOOSAA ILLAA ZURRIYYATUN MIN QAWMEHI A’LAA KHAWF MIN FIR-A’WNA WAMALAA EHEM AN YYAFTENAHUM WA INNA FIR-A’WNA LAA’AALIN FIL ARZE WA INNAHU LAMENAS MUSREFEEN.\nBut believed not in Moses except the posterity of his people (and they were), inspite of (the) fear of Pharaoh and their chiefs, lest he should torment them; and verily, Pharaoh was lofty in the land; and verily, he was of the extravagant.\nوَقَالَ مُوْسٰى يٰقَوْمِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ اٰمَنْتُمْ بِاللّٰهِ فَعَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلُوْاۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّسْلِمِيْنَ‏(84)\nWA QAALA MOOSAA LE-QAWMEHI IN KUNTUM AAMANTUM BIL-LAAHE FA-A’LAYHE TAWAKKALOOA IN KUNTUM MMUSLEMEENA.\nAnd said Moses, “O’ my people! If ye (really) believe in God then on Him (alone) rely (ye) if ye be Muslims.\nفَقَالُوْا عَلَى اللّٰهِ تَوَكَّلْنَا ۚ رَبَّنَا لَا تَجْعَلْنَا فِتْنَةً لِّلْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَۙ‏(85)\nFA-QAALOO A’LAL LAAHE TAWAKKALNAA RABBANAA LAA TAJA’ALNAA FETNATAN LLELQAWME ZAALEMEEN.\nThen said they: “On God (alone) rely! O’ Our Lord! make us not (subject) to a trial from the unjust people.\nوَنَجِّنَا بِرَحْمَتِكَ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(86)\nWANAJJENAA BERAHMATEKA MENAL QAWMIL KAAFEREEN.\nAnd deliver us by Thy mercy from the disbelieving people.\nوَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَىٰ مُوْسٰى وَاَخِيْهِ اَنْ تَبَوَّاٰ لِقَوْمِكُمَا بِمِصْرَ بُيُوْتًا وَّاجْعَلُوْا بُيُوْتَكُمْ قِبْلَةً وَّاَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ ؕ وَبَشِّرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(87)\nWA AWHAYNAA AELAA MOOSAA WA AKHEEHE AN TABAWAAA LEQAWMEKUMAA BEMESRA BUYOOTAN WWAAJA’ALOOA BUYOOTAKUM QIBLATAN WA SALAATA WA BASH-SHERIL MOAMENEEN.\nAnd revealed We unto Moses and his brother (saying) “Take for the people of ye two houses to abide in Egypt and make ye your houses places of worship, and establish ye (regular) prayers; and give glad tidings to the believers.\nوَقَالَ مُوْسٰى رَبَّنَاۤ اِنَّكَ اٰتَيْتَ فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَاَهٗ زِيْنَةً وَّاَمْوَالًا فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ۙ رَبَّنَا لِيُضِلُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِكَۚ رَبَّنَا اطْمِسْ عَلٰٓى اَمْوَالِهِمْ وَاشْدُدْ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ فَلَا يُؤْمِنُوْا حَتّٰى يَرَوُا الْعَذَابَ الْاَ لِيْمَ‏(88)\nWA QAALA MOOSAA RABBANAA INNAKA AATAYTA FIR-A’WNA WAMALAAH ZEENATAN WWAAMWAALAN FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA RABBANAA LEEZELLOOA A’N SABEELEKA RABBANAA ATMES A’LAA AAMWAALEHEM WAASHDUD A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM FALAA YOAMENOO HATTAA YARAWUA A’ZAABA AL-AA LEEMA.\nAnd said (prayed) Moses: “O’ Our Lord! Verily Thou hast given to Pharaoh and his chiefs splendour and riches in the life of this world, (is it) O’ Our Lord! so that they lead (people) astray from Thy path? O’ Our Lord! destroy thou their riches and harden their hearts so that they will believe not until they see the painful chastisement.\nقَالَ قَدْ اُجِيْبَتْ دَّعْوَتُكُمَا فَاسْتَقِيْمَا وَلَا تَتَّبِعٰٓنِّ سَبِيْلَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(89)\nQAALA QAD AUJEEBAT DDAA’WATUKUMAA FAASTAQEEMAA WA LAA TATTABEA’AAANNE SABEELA LAZEENA LAA YA’LAMOON.\nSaid He: “Indeed is accepted the prayer of ye two (O’ Moses and Aaron!) Then keep fast ye two to the right path and follow not ye two the path of those who know not.\nوَجَاوَزْنَا بِبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ الْبَحْرَ فَاَتْبَعَهُمْ فِرْعَوْنُ وَجُنُوْدُهٗ بَغْيًا وَّعَدْوًا ؕ حَتّٰۤى اِذَاۤ اَدْرَكَهُ الْغَرَقُ قَالَ اٰمَنْتُ اَنَّهٗ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا الَّذِىْۤ اٰمَنَتْ بِهٖ بَنُوْۤا اِسْرَآءِيْلَ وَ اَنَا مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(90)\nWAJAAWAZNAA BE-BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ BAHRA FAATBAA’AHUM FIRA’WNO WA JONOODOHU BAGHYAN WWAA’ADWAN HATTAA EZAA AADRAKAHU AL-GHARAQU QAALA AAMANTO ANNAHU LAA ELAAHA ILLAA LAZEE AAAMANAT BEHI BANOOA ISRAAA-EELAZ WA ANAA MENAL AKOONA MENAL MUSLEMEEN.\nAnd caused We the children of Israel to pass (safely) through the sea, then Pharaoh and his hosts chased them in rebellion and hostility; until when drowning overtook him, said (cried) he ‘I believe that there is no God but (He) in Whom the children of Israel believe, and I am of the Muslims’.\nآٰلْئٰنَ وَقَدْ عَصَيْتَ قَبْلُ وَكُنْتَ مِنَ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(91)\nAAAALAANA WA QAD A’ASAYTA QABLO WA KUNTA MENAL MUFSEDEEN.\nWhat! Now! (when facing death?) when thou didst disobey before and thou wast of the mischief-makers.\nفَالْيَوْمَ نُنَجِّيْكَ بِبَدَنِكَ لِتَكُوْنَ لِمَنْ خَلْفَكَ اٰيَةً  ؕ وَاِنَّ كَثِيْرًا مِّنَ النَّاسِ عَنْ اٰيٰتِنَا لَغٰفِلُوْنَ‏(92)\nFALYAWMA NUNAJJEEKA BEBADANEKA LETAKOONA LEMAN-Y KHALFAKA AAYATAL WA INNA KASEERAA MENAL NAASE A’N AAYAATENAA LAGHAAFELOONA.\nBut this day We shall save thee in thy body that thou mayest be after thee a sign (of Ours) unto those who come! But verily many of the people are heedless of Our signs.\nوَلَقَدْ بَوَّاْنَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ مُبَوَّاَ صِدْقٍ وَّرَزَقْنٰهُمْ مِّنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِۚ فَمَا اخْتَلَفُوْا حَتّٰى جَآءَهُمُ الْعِلْمُؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ يَقْضِىْ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فِيْمَا كَانُوْا فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(93)\nWA LAQAD BAWANAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ MUBAWAA SEDQIN WWARAZAQNAAHUM MENAL AT-TAYBAATE FAMAA TALAFOO HATTAA JAAA-AHOMUL AL-E’ELMU INNAL RABBAKA YAQZEE BAYNAHUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE FEEMAA KAANOO FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON.\nAnd indeed We did lodge the children of Israel a true lodging and provided them with good things (for their sustenance); but they differed not until had come unto them the knowledge; verily, thy Lord will judge on the Day of Resurrection in that which they disagreed.\nفَاِنْ كُنْتَ فِىْ شَكٍّ مِّمَّاۤ اَنْزَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ فَسْئَلِ الَّذِيْنَ يَقْرَءُوْنَ الْكِتٰبَ مِنْ قَبْلِكَۚ لَقَدْ جَآءَكَ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ فَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمُمْتَرِيْنَۙ‏(94)\nFA-IN KUNTA FEE SHAKKIM MIMMAA ANZALNAA ELAYKA FASALE LAZEENA YAQRAOONA KETAABA MIN QABLEKA LAQAD JAAA-AKA HAQQO MIN RABBEKA FALAA TAKOONANNA MENAL MUMTAREEN.\nBut if thou art in doubt about what We have sent down unto thee, ask those who read the book (sent) before thee; Indeed the truth hath come unto thee from thy Lord, so be not thou of the doubters.\nوَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ فَتَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(95)\nWA LAA TAKOONANNA MENAL LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE FA TAKOONA MENAL KHAASEREEN.\nNor be thou of those who belied the signs of God (for) then thou shouldst (also) be of the losers.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ حَقَّتْ عَلَيْهِمْ كَلِمَتُ رَبِّكَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَۙ‏(96)\nINNAL LAZEENA HAQQAT A’LAYHIM KALEMATU RABBEKA LAA YOAMENOONA.\nVerily, those against whom the word of thy Lord hath proved true will believe not.\nوَلَوْ جَآءَتْهُمْ كُلُّ اٰيَةٍ حَتّٰى يَرَوُا الْعَذَابَ الْاَ لِيْمَ‏(97)\nWA LAW JAAA-AHUM KULLO AAYATIM HATTAA YARAWUA A’ZAABA AL-AA LEEMA.\nEven if come unto them every sign, until they witness the grievous chastisement.\nفَلَوْلَا كَانَتْ قَرْيَةٌ اٰمَنَتْ فَنَفَعَهَاۤ اِيْمَانُهَاۤ اِلَّا قَوْمَ يُوْنُسَ ۚؕ لَمَّاۤ اٰمَنُوْا كَشَفْنَا عَنْهُمْ عَذَابَ الْخِزْىِ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَمَتَّعْنٰهُمْ اِلٰى حِيْنٍ‏(98)\nFA-LAWLAA KAANAT QARYATUN AAAMANAT FANAFAA’AHAA AEEMAANUHAA ILLAA QAWMA YOONUSA LAMMAA AAMANOO KASHAFNAA A’NHUM A’ZAABAL KHIZYE FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA WAMATTAA’NAAHUM ELAA HEEN.\nAnd why then was there not a town which believed, so its faith should have profited it but the people of Jonah? When they believed We removed from them the torment of ignominy in the life of the world and provided them (with comfort) (to enjoy it) for a fixed while.\nوَلَوْ شَآءَ رَبُّكَ لَاٰمَنَ مَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ كُلُّهُمْ جَمِيْعًا ؕ اَفَاَنْتَ تُكْرِهُ النَّاسَ حَتّٰى يَكُوْنُوْا مُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(99)\nWA LAW SHAAA-AL RABBOKA LAAMANA MAN FIL ARZE KULLUHUM JAMEE-A’A AAFAANTA TUKREHU NAASA HATTAA YAKOONOOA MUMENEENA.\nAnd if hath willed, thy Lord verily all those who are in the earth would have believed, all of them (together); wilt thou then compel people against their will to become believers?\nوَمَا كَانَ لِنَفْسٍ اَنْ تُؤْمِنَ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِؕ وَيَجْعَلُ الرِّجْسَ عَلَى الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(100)\nWA MAA KAANA LE-NAFSIM AN TUMENA ILLAA BE-IZNIL LAAH WAYAJA’ALU A’NKOMUR A’LAL LAZEENA LAA YA’QELOON.\nAnd (although) it is not for any soul to believe except by God’s permission; while casteth He uncleanliness (of infidelity) on those who use not (their) sense.\nقُلِ انْظُرُوْا مَاذَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ ؕ وَمَا تُغْنِى الْاٰيٰتُ وَالنُّذُرُ عَنْ قَوْمٍ لَّا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(101)\nQOLIL ANZUROOA MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA TUGHNEAA AAYAATO WAALNNUZURU A’N QAWMIN LAA YOAMENOONA.\nSay thou, “Observe ye What is in the heavens and earth; but avail not signs and warnings people who believe not.\nفَهَلْ يَنْتَظِرُوْنَ اِلَّا مِثْلَ اَيَّامِ الَّذِيْنَ خَلَوْا مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْؕ قُلْ فَانْتَظِرُوْۤا اِنِّىْ مَعَكُمْ مِّنَ الْمُنْتَظِرِيْنَ‏(102)\nFA HAL YANTAZEROONA ILLAA MISLA AAYAME LAZEENA KHALAW MIN QABLEHIM QUL FAANTAZEROOA INNEE MA-A’KUM MENAL AL-MUNTAZEREENA.\nWhat! wait they then for (any-thing) but the like of the days of those who passed away before them? Say thou “Wait ye then; Verily I too am with you of the waiting ones.\nثُمَّ نُنَجِّىْ رُسُلَنَا وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا كَذٰلِكَۚ حَقًّا عَلَيْنَا نُنْجِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(103)\nSUMMA NUNAJJEAA RUSULANAA WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO KAZAALEKA HAQQAN A’LAYNAA NUNJE MOAMENEEN.\nUltimately (when Our wrath fell) We deliver Our apostles and those who believe - even so it is binding on Us (that) We deliver the believers.\nقُلْ يٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ فِىْ شَكٍّ مِّنْ دِيْنِىْ فَلَاۤ اَعْبُدُ الَّذِيْنَ تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَلٰكِنْ اَعْبُدُ اللّٰهَ الَّذِىْ يَتَوَفّٰٮكُمْ ۖۚ وَاُمِرْتُ اَنْ اَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَۙ‏(104)\nQUL YAA AYYOHAL NAASO IN KUNTUM FEE SHAKKIM MIN DEENEAA FALAA A-A’BODUL LAZEENA TA’BODOONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE WA LAAKIL A-A’BODUL LAAHA LAZEE YATAWAFFAAKUM WA AN A-A’BODA AN SHAY-IWN WA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nSay: “O’ people! If ye be in doubt as to my religion, then (know ye that) I worship not those whom ye worship besides God, but worship I (only) God, Who taketh you away (from this world) and commanded I am that I be of the believers.\nوَاَنْ اَقِمْ وَجْهَكَ لِلدِّيْنِ حَنِيْفًا ۚ وَلَا تَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ‏(105)\nWA AAQEM WAJHAKA LID-DEENIL HANEEFAA WA LAA TAKOONANNA MENAL MUSHREKEEN.\nAnd (I have also been commanded) saying “Set thy face towards religion uprightly and be thou not of the polytheists.\nوَلَا تَدْعُ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا يَنْفَعُكَ وَ لَا يَضُرُّكَۚ فَاِنْ فَعَلْتَ فَاِنَّكَ اِذًا مِّنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(106)\nWA LAA TAD-O’ MIN DOONIL LAAHE MAA LAA YANFAU’UKA WA LAA YAZURRUKA FA-IN FAA’ALTA FA-INNAKA EZAL MENAL ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd call thou not (any one) besides God, that which neither profiteth thee nor harmeth thee; for if thou dost, then (beware!) verily if thou didst it then in that case thou wilt be of the unjust-ones.\nوَاِنْ يَّمْسَسْكَ اللّٰهُ بِضُرٍّ فَلَا كَاشِفَ لَهٗۤ اِلَّا هُوَ ۚ وَاِنْ يُّرِدْكَ بِخَيْرٍ فَلَا رَآدَّ لِفَضْلِهٖ ؕ يُصِيْبُ بِهٖ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖ ؕ وَهُوَ الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(107)\nWA YYAMSASKA LAAHO BEZURRIN FALAA KAASHEFA LAHU ILLAA HOWA WA YYUREDKA BE-KHAYRIN FALAA RAADDA LE-FAZLEHI YUSEEBU BEHI MAN YASHAAA-O MIN E’BAADEHI WA HOWA GHAFOORUL RAHEEM.\nIf God should afflict thee with any harm, then none can be the remover of it but He, and if willeth He any good to thee none can be the repeller of His grace; He bringeth it unto whomsoever He willeth of His servants; and He is the Oft-Forgiving the Merciful.\nقُلْ يٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ قَدْ جَآءَكُمُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّكُمْۚ فَمَنِ اهْتَدٰى فَاِنَّمَا يَهْتَدِىْ لِنَفْسِهٖۚ وَمَنْ ضَلَّ فَاِنَّمَا يَضِلُّ عَلَيْهَاۚ وَمَاۤ اَنَا عَلَيْكُمْ بِوَكِيْلٍؕ‏(108)\nQUL YAA AYYOHAL NAASO QAD JAAAKUMU HAQQO MIN RABBEKUM FAMANE’ TADAA FA-INNAMAA YAHTADEE LENAFSEHI WA MAN ZALLA FA-INNAMAA YAZELLU A’LAYHAA WA MAA ANAA A’LAYKUM BEWAKEELIN.\nSay thou: “O’ ye people! Indeed hath come unto you the truth (Qur’an) from your Lord: therefore whosoever receiveth the guidance, he receiveth the guidance for (the good of) his own self; and whosoever strayeth most surely, he strayeth to the detriment of it; and I am not over you a custodian.\nوَاتَّبِعْ مَا يُوْحٰۤى اِلَيْكَ وَاصْبِرْ حَتّٰى يَحْكُمَ اللّٰهُ ۖۚ وَهُوَ خَيْرُ الْحٰكِمِيْنَ‏(109)\nWAATTABEA’ MAA YOOHAA ELAYKA WAS BIR HATTAA YAHKUMA LAAHO WA HOWA KHAYRUR HAAKEMEEN.\nAnd (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) follow thou what is revealed unto thee and forbear till God giveth judgment; and He is the Best of (all) judges.",
  "merits": "This Surah is ‘Makki’ and it has 109 verses. It is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that if a person recites this Surah once in two or three months, he will not be placed alongside the ignorant ones and will be from among the ‘muqarrabeen’ (close ones) on the Day of Reckoning. It is also narrated that if a person recites Surah Yunus, he will get the reward equal to the number of people who were present in the community of Prophet Yunus (a.s.).\nThis Surah can be used as a means of identifying thieves from among your workers. This is done by either writing the Surah and under it writing the names of all the people in the house or workplace who could be suspected of stealing and then keeping this writing in the house. It will, after some time, become manifest who the thief is."
}
